WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:05.663
- That's legal.

00:00:05.663 --> 00:00:06.720
I can actually come across

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.279
and just whack you as hard as I can.

00:00:08.279 --> 00:00:09.348
You can knock a guy out.

00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:11.040
(speaks in foreign language)
My name is Konishki

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.290
and I am ex-sumotori.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.540
I've been in Japan for the past 40 years.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.220
I joined Sumo 1982,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.680
so I've been in the circuit for 16 years

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.180
as a professional sumotori.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.880
Today, we'll be looking at
some sumo scenes from movies

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.093
and see how real it is to
my eyes, Konishki'e eyes.

00:00:29.031 --> 00:00:34.009
- That man is Mainoumi, the
greatest fighter in Japan

00:00:34.009 --> 00:00:35.730
- [Woman] But he's so tiny.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:36.750
- It's very real.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.830
His name is Mainoumi.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.540
He's actually a real
professional sumotori.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.980
That's the thing that a lot of Americans

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.750
or a lot of foreigners don't know.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.030
The professional Sumo
League, our professional,

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.560
which is only one in the world,

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.820
we don't have any weight class.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.350
It's not wrestling it's,

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.130
it's you just translating
the word into sumo wrestling

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.330
where we call sumotori

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.920
but we don't even call it a sport.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.093
It's more like a culture.

00:00:57.093 --> 00:00:58.770
- Hatakikomi is a movement

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:03.240
smaller combatant uses to throw
the larger man off-balance.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.670
- So like how the actor explained,

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.110
he's going to use a hatakikomi,

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.350
which is a technique used
by a smaller sumotori.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.390
We have like different techniques in sumo

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.970
and the reason for that is
because it's taken advantage

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.230
by the smaller guys.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.900
The bigger guys is
about strength and power

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.970
and then how you move
your weight and stuff.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.770
But the smaller guys that are tricky,

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.543
it's like they kick your
feet, they pull your hands,

00:01:24.543 --> 00:01:25.830
they twist your elbows

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.420
and it's very dangerous.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.780
And salt is used very much
in the Japanese culture.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.840
If you go through many
shrines or temples in Japan,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.448
you are gonna notice that
there's certain places

00:01:35.448 --> 00:01:37.410
they put salt just to purify.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.570
And there's a thing in
the Japanese culture,

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.250
when you go to someone's funeral,

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.470
when you go back they
give you these envelopes,

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.640
there's salt in it.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.520
So what it does is chase away bad spirits

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.170
before you walk into your home.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.210
And sumotoris use the salt

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.620
to actually bless their
rings every single day

00:01:54.652 --> 00:01:56.073
- [Man] Look, there.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.010
- The hair you see during that tournament

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.220
they call it "oicho."

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.120
Oicho is for only high rankers.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.700
What we regularly wear is what
you see the samurai movies

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.650
like "Chonmage."

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:08.610
If you go bald,

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.470
I notice they're doing extensions.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.290
This is why you can separate the sumotori

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.750
from any other professional sport

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.430
because we have to dress like them.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:18.810
You're not allowed to wear any of these.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.160
You get caught wearing something else,

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.110
they probably kick you out right away.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.510
So you have to walk the
streets with kimonos

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.343
during the winter

00:02:25.343 --> 00:02:27.420
and then yokota, what we call
it, is a lighter material

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.120
and we have to wear what
setters are called slippers.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.550
The setters we wear, we
can tell what rank you are

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.467
just by looking at the wrap
and from the slippers you wear.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.630
It's a pull down.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.510
This technique is used
by a smaller opponent

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.850
because it's all about speed and timing.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.590
But all he's trying to
do is just to beat you

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.120
to make you come forward

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.400
and push your weight forward fast enough

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.233
where he can time it,

00:02:51.233 --> 00:02:53.250
where he just throw the
(beep) at you and stuff.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.740
So that take dig itself is well used.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.780
I wouldn't use it because
by the time I do it,

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.710
they probably hit my belly

00:02:58.710 --> 00:02:59.850
because I'm pulling down.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:04.100
It's a very winning move
for that type of sumotori.

00:03:05.414 --> 00:03:06.600
This is such a cool clip.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.180
The way you see it the dohyo,
which is the sumo ring.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.400
If you look at the way
that it's built those days

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.860
they used to have the poles on the corner

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.880
to hold up the top.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.740
During my career, we still had that,

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.440
not in a major tournament
but between our tours.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.500
The thing I like about the
scene, it makes it so like,

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.500
authentic the way they built that stadium.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.120
I would like to see it go back to that

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.057
and make it lesser

00:03:28.057 --> 00:03:29.070
because right now you got to imagine

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.500
we have six major
tournaments a year in Japan

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.350
and there's 12,000 people
there, 15 days in a row.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.340
And that is crazy

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.741
because they're using two real sumotoris

00:03:37.741 --> 00:03:39.210
and this is beautiful.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.320
I think I give them a 10.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.090
I wish I could wrestle that era.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:44.250
The way it's built around the ring itself

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.833
and very authentic.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:51.683
What you just seen

00:03:51.683 --> 00:03:53.520
is exactly what they were
doing in that tournament

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:54.810
or during the match.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.730
They have a thing what
we call, "chirichozu,"

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:59.070
which is they come up
and they do the ceremony

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.140
where they slap their
hands and they do all this.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.910
This is another tradition

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.040
that for us to respect our opponent

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.890
to show him that I left
my double barrel at home.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:08.723
I ain't going to shoot you,

00:04:08.723 --> 00:04:10.380
I'm going to beat you
up with my own hands.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.580
It's that kind of thing.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.320
The referee doesn't say (beep).

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.060
He gotta touch all fours.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.290
The hands have to touch.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.550
He uses eye contact

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.980
so that's what makes
sumos very unique too.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.780
If you're running a hundred yard dash,

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.140
somebody pushed the guns
or even a boxing match,

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.160
the bell rings right?

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.493
But this is all eye contact.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.580
It's a funny clip.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.530
The motions and everything is kind of real

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:39.570
but the throws are, that wouldn't happen.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:43.050
They would only happen in a superman move.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.250
Those throwing techniques

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.800
that you're going to see
some guys get flip flipped,

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.780
like, back flipped like, you know.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:49.860
That can really happen.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.860
The word for what technique
they used, kimarite,

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.790
means is today's match
kimarite, is he forced out.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:59.873
Kimarite is just the meaning of that.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.700
That is very real.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.130
One of these two guys are
supposed to be a grand champion.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.840
If you're grand champion,
you get (beep) kicked.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.970
So people would actually
throw the zabutons.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.850
It's those pillows that they
sit on at the tournaments

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.680
and you see this even till today.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.520
It's tradition.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.460
The people watching on the
side on the floor get hurt.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.660
Some people think it's just good luck

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.580
even though they go to the
hospital with broken bones.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.950
But because sumotoris are trained so well,

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.270
we learn how to break falls.

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:26.220
No one really gets hurt
falling off the ring.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.830
Everything is more like
elbow or twisted knees.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.260
A six or seven, 6.5.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.010
7 is good, it's good.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:39.773
Very, very good.

00:05:39.773 --> 00:05:42.330
The guy who has the fan is
what we call a "yobidashi,"

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.620
which is a ring caller.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.140
The other guy who has
the panel in his hand

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:48.270
is called "gyoji," which is the referee.

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:50.280
Every sumo stable has one of each.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.740
Those positions too are ranked.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.110
You have like from the lowest
rank to the highest rank.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.310
The drums would never be there.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.676
But that's the only, only
thing that I wouldn't see

00:05:58.676 --> 00:06:01.093
in a regular sumo tournament.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.510
That is very normal.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.580
The shiko is the squatting that they do

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:09.990
where they lift up their legs

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.130
and pound their legs down.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.390
That's what they call "shiko."

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:13.620
So that's the sumo squat.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.690
That's what they do to
stomp away the bad spirits

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:16.523
on the ring.

00:06:16.523 --> 00:06:19.440
In your first six months,
all you do is shiko.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.810
You do like a thousand a day, easy.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.120
That's the best exercise
to strengthen your legs

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.980
and actually strengthen up your core.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.320
But I think because of
the exercises we do,

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.550
it help prevents injuries.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.320
It loosen up your hips
and stuff like that.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.441
You can get lower.

00:06:32.441 --> 00:06:35.640
(crowd cheering)

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.190
This is exactly what you
would see at at a sumo match.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:39.030
Actually we can go

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.280
and actually broke your elbow in one move.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:42.930
What the guy just did, he can step out

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.070
and what we do,

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.130
use my elbow to clamp down
on his hand that's on me.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.990
And all after these
twist in and twist down,

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:49.950
I can break his elbow.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:51.450
So my fingers all broken from that

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:53.850
because we learn how to
cut your hand off the belt

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:54.990
when you grab it.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:56.520
And there's like four
or five different ways

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.543
to kick the belt off your hand.

00:06:57.543 --> 00:07:00.626
It's very easy to break your fingers.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:03.473
That's legal.

00:07:03.473 --> 00:07:04.650
I can actually come across

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.210
and just whack you as hard as I can.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.670
You can knock a guy out
cause it's a karate chop.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.130
The mix of martial arts,
aikido, and karate.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.630
And actually I can brake your nose

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:14.100
with my hand, with my palm,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.660
which I did during my career.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.243
So people don't know that part.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:22.200
To win a sumo match is simple.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.480
It's 5.5 meters, that round circle.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.460
You have 5.5 meters to work with.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.600
So the object of the game

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.670
is to push your opponent out of the ring

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.930
or throw him into the ring.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.810
Anything but the bottom of
his feet touches the floor,

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:34.710
you lose the match.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.090
So it sounds easy,

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:37.980
but having guys over 400 pound

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.420
going against each other, pushing weight,

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.240
they can try to take
advantage of weight shifting

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.073
and stuff like that.

00:07:43.073 --> 00:07:44.730
It's not as easy as it looks.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.440
I would rate it a nine,

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.850
it's just the jumps
that took a point away.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.430
But it's a very good clip.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:53.347
(speaking in foreign language)

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:00.600
That's the ranking,

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.550
since the second highest is the champion.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.890
Before they had grand champion, Yokozuna,

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:08.250
the only the highest rank was
only Ozeki in the olden days.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.140
Never been done by any foreigner, bro.

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:11.460
I'm the first to ever do that

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.860
and it's a shocking to the sumo world

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.770
or to the country because
no one has done it before

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:19.170
and I was very fortunate
to be in the right time,

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:23.493
right place, right mind,
physical to handle the sport.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:27.450
(speaking in foreign language)

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:28.860
It's the best protein.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:29.970
Call it "chankinabe."

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.410
That's how they put our weight on.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.838
It's very, very nutritious.

00:08:32.838 --> 00:08:34.560
Very, very healthy too.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.170
It can be chicken, can
be pork, it can be beef,

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.790
can be a mixture of different meats,

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.710
can be fish, seafood.

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.670
So that changes every single day.

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:43.849
You don't have the same menu at all.

00:08:43.849 --> 00:08:44.970
And you have to be very healthy

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:47.160
because they check on your
body if you're diabetic

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.360
or they won't take you.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.700
They check your heart
every like twice a year.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:53.250
They're very crucial about being healthy

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.200
'cause to be big and to grow bigger,

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.580
you have to have a healthy body

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:58.042
to handle all the eating too.

00:08:58.042 --> 00:09:03.042
(speaking in foreign language)

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:06.965
You got a 10 on that one.

00:09:06.965 --> 00:09:08.100
He's actually getting introduced

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.660
to a stable that he's gonna join.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:13.110
You are guest until you
come officially a sumotori.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:16.170
So he's getting treated as a VIP

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:17.520
which everybody get treated.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:18.390
If you're not a sumotori

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.490
and you're invited to
come to a sumo stable,

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:21.323
get used to it

00:09:21.323 --> 00:09:23.143
because they'll be serving
you until you leave.

00:09:23.143 --> 00:09:27.390
(speaking in foreign language)

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:28.560
It's a building bro.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:29.430
Everybody lives there

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:30.593
and everything is in there.

00:09:30.593 --> 00:09:32.430
Their practice area is in there.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:33.750
The shower rooms are huge.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.010
The kitchens are huge.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.470
They actually can make their
sumo stables into restaurants

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:38.310
if they wanted to.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:39.960
Everybody sleep on futons.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:41.370
Even that is by ranking too.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:42.930
So the higher rank have their own room.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.280
I had my own room to sleep in.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:46.170
But the lower rank, they
all sleep in one room.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.610
So it's real.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:50.153
What you just saw is exactly what happens.

00:09:50.153 --> 00:09:53.516
(upbeat music)

00:09:53.516 --> 00:09:57.433
(speaking in foreign language)

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:00.030
- A million percent right.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.710
You have to be the first to get up,

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.720
get people's stuff prepared.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:05.220
You've got to be the last to go to sleep

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.440
because you're taking
people's stuff to wash

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:08.760
and you've got to make sure everybody,

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.980
your senior guys have their towels,

